HST Office: formulas saved to .docx (and .rtf) look in Word as they do in HST Writer.

Word showed these differences in every formula saved from StarMath to OMML (.docx):
- Function names (sin, cos, log, lim, "func det") were italic. An OMML run is italic unless its
  m:rPr has m:sty m:val="p" (ECMA-376 Part 1, 22.1.2.112); a StarMath function name (text in
  the function font, upright) now gets that property. Variables keep Word's italic.
  RTF math writes the same as \msty0 (RTF math control words are the OMML names).
- A function name ran into its argument ("sinx"): Word only spaces them inside m:func, and the
  argument of a StarMath function is not a node of its own. A thin space (U+2009) run marked
  m:sty "p" follows the name (after its scripts, as in cos^2); the import drops exactly that
  run, so the formula text does not change on a round trip. lim is m:func already.
- The text of an arrow with text ("{t} xrightarrow {}", reaction conditions) sat on the
  baseline with a small arrow hanging under it. The group (m:groupChr, text as the base, arrow
  under it) was written with m:vertJc "top", which puts the top part on the baseline (22.1.2.117);
  an arrow with text now writes "bot" (OMML and RTF), so the arrow stays on the baseline like a
  relation and its text sits above, as StarMath lays it out. Braces keep their values.
- Matrix columns aligned with alignl/alignr (cases, aligned) were centred, and a .docx round
  trip lost the alignment. The matrix now writes m:mPr/m:mcs with one m:mc (m:count 1, m:mcJc)
  per column when a column is not centred, from the alignment the formula's layout gives its
  cells; import reads m:mcJc (repeated m:count times) back as alignl/alignr cells.
- Stack rows aligned left (systems, \begin{array}{l}) were centred: Word centres m:eqArr rows,
  and its alignment points (m:aln) line rows up with each other, not with the left edge. A stack
  whose rows are all aligned left (or right) is written as a one-column m:m with that m:mcJc and
  read back as the stack. Other stacks and the lines of a formula stay m:eqArr.
- A matrix row whose first cell was empty lost its column separator on import.

The logic is in starmath/source/hst/ommllayout.cxx; the export and import get one call each.
MathType OLE objects that are not converted are not StarMath objects and are written unchanged.

Test: CppunitTest_starmath_qa_cppunit (test_hst_omml_layout.cxx) checks the OMML and RTF
written for each case and reads the OMML back.

